# Decision Record: XADD Entry Point and Snapshot Iteration

The first record for 2023-03-15 started with a file, not a confirmed public class name. The starting point was `jctools-core/src/main/java/org/jctools/queues/BaseMpscLinkedArrayQueue.java`, which the repository index placed in the existing java module for code reading and historical behavior checks.

The local relationships visible at the top of the file at the time were:

```java
package org.jctools.queues;
import org.jctools.queues.IndexedQueueSizeUtil.IndexedQueue;
import org.jctools.util.PortableJvmInfo;
import org.jctools.util.Pow2;
```

The search results also included `chunks`, `org`, `jctools`, `queues`, `int`, and `chunk`. This was enough to make it a starting point worth revisiting, but not enough to establish it as the place where XADD's public identity was defined. The early notes put "the file shows chunk relationships" and "which queue users should instantiate" too close together; that judgment is left as recorded for now.

At the time, there were two options: continue tracing `BaseMpscLinkedArrayQueue`'s inheritance relationships to write an overview, or keep only the file path and look elsewhere for a stable public name. The latter was chosen. The path is retained for `internal/jctools-core` as a `v_prev` navigation point; it must not be promoted to a public entry point based solely on index terms.

MPSC Snapshot Iterator was not documented as confirmed behavior in this version either. Reproduction needs to start from the pre-call state, followed by a check for any additional visible changes after the action completes. Leave blanks where there are no results yet; do not turn the presence of chunks directly into a conclusion about the iterator.

This version's decision is to record "queue identity", "base file", and "snapshot iterator observations" separately.
